1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:02,400
You win!

2
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:08,337
Tomorrow's battle will
be the final showdown.

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:11,397
We'll be launching a surprise
attack from the rear.

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:15,397
Once the Fortified City's forces
slow down the Combined Stratum Lords,

5
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,557
they'll send the signal for us to begin.

6
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,934
Does that about sum it all up, Hayachi?

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,000
Yep. Don't you worry.

8
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:25,377
The Guardian will certainly be able
to keep the Stratum Lords busy.

9
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:28,107
As for how, you'll just
have to wait and see.

10
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:31,317
They sure have a lot of faith
in this guardian of theirs.

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,635
I guess we should believe in him, too.

12
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:37,517
And once the Netherlord shows
his ugly mug, that'll be our cue.

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,894
That's when we strike.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,765
It'll be up to us to get rid of
the Netherlord once and for all.

15
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,987
Does anyone have anything
they'd like to say?

16
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:46,990
I do.

17
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,237
I've got something I've been
wanting to get off my chest.

18
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,337
We surrendered ourselves to
the Netherlord once before.

19
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,397
For that, we should have died.

20
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:58,037
I wanted to thank you from the bottom
of my heart for taking us back.

21
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:02,238
Even if this battle's the end of the
line for us, I've got no regrets.

22
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,520
I feel the same way, my dear.

23
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,822
Our son's curse has been lifted.

24
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,037
There's nothing more I could ask for.

25
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:10,950
Yeah.

26
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:12,977
I get that you guys are pumped about this.

27
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,397
We definitely don't have
any plans to die here.

28
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,310
Right, Akka?

29
00:01:16,393 --> 00:01:17,357
You can say that again.

30
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:21,037
There's no way I'm dying before I get a
girlfriend and we make out sloppy style.

31
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:25,157
You getting worked up for something so
pathetic makes me ashamed to be your brother.

32
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,280
Don't pay those fools any mind,
Kai. You have me. Damn it!

33
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,180
Let's do this!

34
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,417
Come on, everyone!

35
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,217
We'll burn bright until we burn out!

36
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,320
Not so fast now.

37
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,137
It doesn't burning out mean you die.

38
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:40,837
The captain's right, but we
should try to come back alive.

39
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,237
Don't just assume we won't.

40
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:47,060
Anyway, I suppose we should just do
what we always do then. Good idea.

41
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:50,577
We need to be around to watch our
granddaughter grow up, after all.

42
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:53,140
I would follow Master Boxo anywhere,

43
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,077
even if it meant marching
straight into Hell itself.

44
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,042
We vow to stand steadfast
by the Guardian's side.

45
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:01,240
Isn't that right, Usata? Usarion?

46
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:04,860
If anyone gets hurt, let me know.

47
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,237
I'll patch you up.

48
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:09,017
With the Director on our side, as
long as you're still breathing,

49
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,957
you'll be back in the fight in no time.

50
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,337
We'll be firing a ton of arrows,
so I don't want anyone getting hit.

51
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,017
And Pity will do her best. Promise.

52
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:21,637
As for me, I'll be driving an A-car around
with Shui and the director on board.

53
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,720
If you get hurt, I'll pick you up.

54
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,350
All right!

55
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:28,699
Wait, is it just me or is
something coming this way?

56
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,726
Hold on a sec, that's Botong.

57
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,528
And he's got people in tow!

58
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:39,317
My goodness, I thought that was it for me.

59
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,282
Thank you, you were a huge help.

60
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,057
Forgive me, God.

61
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,080
It's been far too long
since I prayed to you.

62
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,940
It's Director Baron Heavy.

63
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,597
I thought both of you were
at the Fortified City.

64
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,510
What happened?

65
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,220
It's the final showdown.

66
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:58,757
Instead of hiding away in the city,
we wanted to fight beside you all.

67
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,657
Also, you would have run
into trouble without me.

68
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,570
Not really.

69
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:04,440
We were fine. Right, Akka?

70
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:05,877
Yep, that's right, Shiro.

71
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,077
I'd even forgotten that you weren't here.

72
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,217
I've got the director by
my side, so I'm good to go.

73
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:12,653
You should have stayed.

74
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,682
Why'd you come?

75
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:15,970
Ah!

76
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:23,320
Team Poxo is finally all back together!

77
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,719
Um, I was gonna say something,
but I totally forgot!

78
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,158
Anyway, let's do our best, everyone!

79
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:31,717
Everybody's full of determination!

80
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,157
And they're plenty enthused!

81
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:36,240
All that's left is for the
final showdown to begin!

82
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:49,717
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

83
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,237
In this new world of wonders,

84
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:54,857
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas!

85
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:56,900
The name's Boxxo. Hello there!

86
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,740
That means yes, by the way!

87
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,217
What are you, I mean to get it!

88
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,957
Going in to almost as a mission.

89
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:21,577
I need to stop by listening.

90
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:26,697
But you want to learn both of us,
Be able to do some of our tasks!

91
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:27,610
You know you don't know what it is?

92
00:04:27,693 --> 00:04:28,523
Where the laughs, driving!

93
00:04:28,606 --> 00:04:29,780
I am so much!

94
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,197
I have your sights.

95
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,580
Okay, I understand.

96
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,070
I'm so strict!

97
00:04:34,153 --> 00:04:34,983
I am so strict!

98
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:35,896
You're the ultimate!

99
00:04:35,979 --> 00:04:36,809
I'm in love.

100
00:04:36,892 --> 00:04:38,300
You're the ultimate!

101
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,020
You're the ultimate!

102
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,937
Oh?

103
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,726
The destined day has arrived.

104
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:17,657
Our job today is to thin out
that tidal wave of monsters and

105
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:21,211
then defeat the huge frankenfreak
of stratum lord thingies.

106
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,460
This spot looks good.

107
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,977
What's up to all the
life forms in the soil?

108
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,117
It's nice to meet you.

109
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,200
My name is Field.

110
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:33,444
Sorry to harsh your buzz
and jam myself in here.

111
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,857
I'd like to have a little
chat with you if that's okay.

112
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:40,646
I don't mean to interrupt, but
is this really necessary, Field?

113
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:44,157
I don't actually have any
proof that it does anything.

114
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,137
But it feels easier to
manipulate the soil when I do it.

115
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,220
I had no idea.

116
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,037
I learned something new today.

117
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,179
Truth is, it's a mystery to me too.

118
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:55,146
I just kind of feel my
way through this stuff.

119
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,550
Awesome!

120
00:05:56,633 --> 00:05:58,237
I have the land's permission.

121
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:00,379
So now I can go as crazy as I want.

122
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,500
Let's see here.

123
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:03,477
Where's the big fused up batty?

124
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,677
Of course, it's standing way in the back.

125
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:08,717
I couldn't ask for a more
perfect setup in my plan.

126
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,388
Time to get things started.

127
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,724
First I'll surprise them
with a little pit stop!

128
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:16,138
Have a nice trip, see you next fall!

129
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:19,322
I'll take my time consuming
those monsters later!

130
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,480
Too bad, they're nutrients now!

131
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,618
It's finally decided to bust a move!

132
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:34,077
Check out the size of that thing though!

133
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,780
How do I want to do this?

134
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,717
The vending machine
gang's probably watching

135
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:40,257
so I might as well put on a show for them!

136
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,987
So this is how I'll stop it!

137
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,330
Hiya!

138
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,800
Wap-a-chow!

139
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,480
Take that!

140
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,340
I'm not gonna let up!

141
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:59,931
Tell me, monster, can you smell
what this field is cooking?

142
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,420
What the heck?

143
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,757
My circuits can't handle
what's happening here!

144
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:08,597
Right now, the ground has arms
and legs, and it's fist fighting!

145
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,620
This makes no sense.

146
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,394
Matt's kind of creepy.

147
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:16,140
I thought so too, but I
didn't come out and say it.

148
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,517
Oh, wow, look at the Guardian go.

149
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,718
He's as dashing and gallant as ever.

150
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:24,117
Yeah, I had a feeling that was
Field taking care of business.

151
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,797
Now I feel kind of
silly for ever stressing

152
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,409
out over being reborn
as a vending machine.

153
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,197
Wait, is he making all
those pits appear too?

154
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,692
Yup, that's one of the Guardian's powers.

155
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:34,970
For real?

156
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,817
That's another thing Field can do?

157
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:37,997
This is no time for gawking.

158
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,904
We still have a job to do here!

159
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,660
You could even win a reward!

160
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,975
Fields taken on the Combined
Stratum Lord, Mano Alando.

161
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:51,062
Plus, he swallowed up a
bunch of the little guys.

162
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:54,057
First things first, we
need to open up a path.

163
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,260
Dance, O' Fire!

164
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,140
Shriek, O' Wind!

165
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,440
Oh, yeah!

166
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,291
This looks like my stuff!

167
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,700
Go on ahead!

168
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,942
He's charging it all by himself?

169
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:08,817
I know the director is strong, but
isn't that a little too reckless?

170
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,429
We're staying behind, too.

171
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,997
If someone doesn't stop
this horde of monsters here,

172
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,357
they'll get in your way when
you take on the Netherlord.

173
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:16,897
We're counting on you, Boxo!

174
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,810
Come back!

175
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:21,000
You got this! Kick his butt!

176
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:24,740
We'll be fine.

177
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:27,860
We'll see them again,
won't we? Hello there.

178
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,197
I'm not the only one who's anxious.

179
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,221
Guys, you better come back alive!

180
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:38,197
We need to stay focused
on the task at hand.

181
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:41,837
Even without his army, the
Netherlord won't be easy to defeat.

182
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:42,750
He's right.

183
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:46,725
They drew a ton of enemies away,
but there are still a ton left.

184
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,600
I must apologize.

185
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,577
We'll be stopping here to
give the Guardian a hand.

186
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:54,307
I wish you the best of luck!

187
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:01,377
And just like that, she's off.

188
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,897
It seems my sister is as restless as ever.

189
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:06,580
I'm sure her group will manage just fine.

190
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:09,252
Here's hoping everything goes as planned.

191
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,340
Hey, it's the Netherlord.

192
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,737
He's looking this way.

193
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,620
We did cause a big hubbub.

194
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,617
It makes sense he'd take notice of us.

195
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,240
How infuriating.

196
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:23,257
Thanks to your tiresome meddling,
my plans have been foiled again.

197
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,400
You will pay for your insolence.

198
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:29,187
It's pretty obvious from his
voice that he's pissed off at us.

199
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:40,520
He seems so angry, I couldn't resist
launching that to add some flair.

200
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:44,317
Flowers of light blooming on
the battlefield is a nice touch.

201
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,580
Very interesting.

202
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:48,140
Even now, you continue to mock me?

203
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,397
I actually thought it might calm you down.

204
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,310
Whoopsie!

205
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:56,717
My loyal servants, heed my call
and return from the path to Hades.

206
00:09:56,800 --> 00:10:02,280
Master the power of the Netherlord and
punish these fools to defy your master!

207
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:13,547
Wait, those are the
Pinky and Thumb Generals!

208
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:19,894
And that's the Forefinger General,
but I defeated him back in the forest!

209
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,117
It looks like the Netherlord sacrificed a

210
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,537
bunch of monsters so he
could bring them back.

211
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,420
Three general class baddies.

212
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:29,954
If the Netherlord jumps in
two, we won't stand a chance.

213
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,088
I suppose it's time for
us to make our move.

214
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:34,517
It sure looks that way.

215
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,237
When's the last time we fought together?

216
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,057
It must have been forever in a day.

217
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:38,970
How do you know?

218
00:10:39,053 --> 00:10:40,657
The Black Band is back together.

219
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:44,577
I never would have thought we'd get
a chance to team up like this again.

220
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,719
Seems long life has its advantages.

221
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:51,117
We'll take care of the three generals.

222
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,820
The Netherlord is all yours. Hold on!

223
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:57,237
Those guys are way too strong for
you to challenge them by yourselves.

224
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,202
We'll help you.

225
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,357
Yeah, she's right.

226
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,057
We should all be fighting together.

227
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:02,905
Sorry, but I can't allow that.

228
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:06,557
If the Netherlord were to unleash his magic
while we're in the middle of our battle,

229
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,934
we'd all be wiped out.

230
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:12,637
Because of that, someone needs to fight
him directly, or else we're sure to lose.

231
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:16,997
Everyone knows that it's up to seniors
like us to put on the boring opening act.

232
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:20,457
It's only right for us to let the
next generation take the spotlight.

233
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,777
If only I were 40 years younger,

234
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:26,357
I would have insisted on battling
it out with the Netherlord myself.

235
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,557
Ah, that really brings back memories.

236
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:31,577
The two of you were always so
hot-blooded back in the day.

237
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:33,540
Man, getting old sucks, huh?

238
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,557
One second, you're the main attraction,

239
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:38,337
but in the blink of an
eye, you're just sidekicks.

240
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,250
There you go.

241
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:41,460
There's no need to worry about us.

242
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,457
Also, I don't need to hear any
more complaining about getting old.

243
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:47,357
We were trying to be considerate,

244
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:50,852
but it seems we were just being
rude by worrying too much.

245
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,447
Don't have to tell me twice.

246
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,438
We're leaving the rest to you, Voxo.

247
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:59,561
Make sure you keep everyone safe.

248
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:01,700
Hello there.

249
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:05,610
Voxo!

250
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:13,437
When he summoned his generals, the
Netherlord probably used up a bunch of mana.

251
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,520
You can take him.

252
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,580
Activate Barrier!

253
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:29,377
The game plan is for
me to focus on defense.

254
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:31,697
and buy time while we wait
for the reinforcements?

255
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,192
from the fortified city.

256
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:37,960
Judging by how strong Field
is, the plan should work.

257
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:41,577
I'm guessing the Netherlord
understands that too.

258
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:44,580
I don't have time to
waste on you, sorry lot.

259
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:47,054
I'm going to settle this farce quickly.

260
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:48,977
Looks like someone's impatient.

261
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:53,295
For some reason, he's skipping his
usual routine of belittling us first.

262
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,120
What the heck?

263
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:10,751
He's created some kind of mini black hole.

264
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,312
There, you're wide open.

265
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:16,457
That won't save you.

266
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:20,580
My darkness sphere sucks everything
up into the spirit world.

267
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:23,116
It's impossible for you to resist it.

268
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:26,717
Sounds like he found a spell that
lets him get past my barrier.

269
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,460
Hold on, that's really bad.

270
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,360
What should we do now? I don't know.

271
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:33,380
Seriously, what do we do?

272
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,540
Crap, we're in big trouble.

273
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:44,960
Hey, Boxo!

274
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:52,140
You have to get bigger that
way you won't get sucked up.

275
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,181
Oh, that's right

276
00:13:57,520 --> 00:14:03,260
Try picking me up now nether nerd you
must think you've outsmarted me with that?

277
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,552
This isn't looking good.

278
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,340
Now this is a problem.

279
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:20,960
This is looking bad.

280
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,880
Isn't there anything we can do? No!

281
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:27,260
Master Foxo! Not good. It's not good!

282
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,780
We're getting abducted!

283
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:34,440
I hope you enjoy your
journey to the spirit world!

284
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,100
How are the others doing?

285
00:14:58,840 --> 00:14:59,670
Nice.

286
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:01,477
They're totally crushing it.

287
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,972
I might as well wrap things up here, too.

288
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:08,920
Chase Bielder!

289
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:16,780
All right, time to cook on the
final dish with maximum destruction.

290
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:19,177
I've decided to make some rock skewers.

291
00:15:19,260 --> 00:15:22,577
Our main ingredient is a big
fresh rock in the shape of a dog.

292
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:25,280
And the skewer is gonna be yours truly.

293
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:33,537
I'll make a point out of
selectively bred burdock roots.

294
00:15:33,620 --> 00:15:36,937
Thanks to generations of careful
breeding, I've created this masterpiece?

295
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:39,314
that's even harder than tempered steel.

296
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,520
What's more?

297
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:47,597
If I use vines to add a truckload of
torque to the already ultra-heavy tip,

298
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,917
it'll at least double the skewering power.

299
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,800
Or I think that's what
I read in a manga once.

300
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,540
This is the spirit world?

301
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,487
It looks like the
aftermath of an apocalypse.

302
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,857
There's not a single living thing here.

303
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,800
This place feels so lonely.

304
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:14,260
How am I supposed to find
tasty food to eat in here?

305
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,640
This is scary.

306
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:16,940
I don't like it.

307
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:20,157
In a world devoid of people,
there can be no footwear.

308
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,240
What a nightmare.

309
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:25,537
I was expecting there to be more of the
Netherlord's minions running around.

310
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:26,679
Guess I was wrong.

311
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,680
What do we do?

312
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:29,700
Psst. Uh-oh. Time.

313
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,757
We can't wait around
for something to happen.

314
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:36,780
We have to hurry and get back.

315
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:41,600
No need to worry about that, because
you'll all be dead soon enough.

316
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:42,660
The Netherlord.

317
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,640
Cooking complete.

318
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,100
Too bad for you,

319
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,277
but one of the main
reasons you lost is that

320
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:56,831
you didn't have enough fiber in your diet.

321
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,880
Well done, Field!

322
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:07,140
Yeah, you really knocked him dead.

323
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,973
You're as amazing as ever, Sir Guardian.

324
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:14,533
I guess Hayachi snuck in at
some point during the battle.

325
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,440
Everyone did well.

326
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:22,702
Let's have a victory party
once this is all over.

327
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:24,560
Wait a sec.

328
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:27,172
I don't see Boxxo in the others anywhere.

329
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:28,360
Boxxo, huh?

330
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,857
That's the name of that
vending machine guy.

331
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:33,537
I thought they were supposed
to be fighting the Netherlord.

332
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:35,208
Where the heck did they go?

333
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,735
Did they get magic to weigh somewhere?

334
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,077
Huh? Huh?

335
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,395
Look there, Guardian!

336
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,774
Something's happening!

337
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:52,450
It's back!

338
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:56,697
As long as the Netherlord is alive,
it looks like it'll keep reviving.

339
00:17:56,780 --> 00:18:01,074
He's the one controlling it, so it
makes sense he's got to go down first.

340
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,055
Jace, this is a real pain in the butt.

341
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,317
We'll have to take care
of this thing first.

342
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,417
We'll leave the Netherlord to you guys.

343
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:12,147
As a fellow otherworldly traveler,
I have faith in you, Boxxo.

344
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:18,160
You trapped us in here.

345
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,417
Why'd you bother coming in?

346
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,480
Yes, yes.

347
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:23,877
I'll take this opportunity
to finish you off.

348
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:26,784
That magic item in
particular must be destroyed.

349
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:30,627
I won't allow something that
exceeds my expectations to exist.

350
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:31,640
I see.

351
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:35,317
So he followed us in here to make sure
I was destroyed for good this time.

352
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:36,518
Isn't that special?

353
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,140
So if we beat you here,

354
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:41,037
it'll help out everybody else
who's fighting on the other side.

355
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:41,950
She's right.

356
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:45,020
Let's kick the skeleton's
big bony butt. Yeah.

357
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:46,800
He's done for.

358
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:48,520
We'll bury him here.

359
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:52,997
You must be punished for sending me to a
world without a single piece of footwear.

360
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:55,780
With this, I'll sever
our cursed connection.

361
00:18:56,120 --> 00:19:00,560
If I so desired, I could simply
crush you like insects right now.

362
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:06,060
That portal links back to your world.

363
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:09,080
And upon my death, it will become active.

364
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:11,322
That should serve as motivation.

365
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:15,617
Nice of him to do that, but who
knows if it's just another trick.

366
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:17,917
You guys try to keep the Netherlord busy.

367
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,757
While you're fighting, I'll investigate
to see if that portal's legit.

368
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:23,680
I wouldn't waste my time lying to you.

369
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:27,457
While I resent the fact that you've
thwarted my plans again and again,

370
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,240
in my view, it makes you worthy foes.

371
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:35,060
Because of that, you will have the
distinct honor of dying by my hand.

372
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:36,496
That's a good point.

373
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:39,917
He may be an evil skeleton hellbent
on conquering the whole world,

374
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,680
but he's never lied to us.

375
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:43,600
If we were to fight here,

376
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:48,055
your concern for that woman would
keep you from fully using your powers.

377
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,912
Changing things up, huh?

378
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,997
You're not hiding behind
hostages or traps anymore?

379
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:04,657
I've decided the best way to defeat you is

380
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,387
to utterly crush you
with overwhelming power.

381
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:11,895
That way you won't be able to say you
only lost because of dirty tricks.

382
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,560
Now, attack me however you'd like.

383
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:20,157
Because I'm feeling generous,
I promise not to fight back.

384
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:23,520
I'll let you experience true despair.

385
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:26,760
Fine!

386
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:28,560
Ready or not, here I come!

387
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:50,280
You wield considerable power,
But unfortunately for you,

388
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:53,520
it's not enough to shatter
the barrier of darkness.

389
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,592
Considerable power, huh?

390
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:59,720
He can tell how strong it was even
though it didn't leave a scratch.

391
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:05,469
Let's see if you can handle
this one through Rolling Strike!

392
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:22,151
I wonder if he can see his mana depleting.

393
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:25,757
Kind of like when my points go down
whenever my barrier takes a hit.

394
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:29,277
Standing here and simply taking
your attacks is getting dull.

395
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:31,831
Perhaps I should have a little bit of fun.

396
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:33,000
Come on, now.

397
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:35,717
Did you forget what you said
about not fighting back?

398
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:38,340
Unless our attacks are actually working?

399
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,840
Fighting back!

400
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:43,577
Oh, don't flatter yourself.

401
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:46,280
I've just grown tired of waiting. Too bad!

402
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:51,757
I can tell he's glaring at me with
those beady little light balls.

403
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:54,840
Maybe I should cool it with
the taunting for a bit!

404
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,497
Guess it's his turn to attack now.

405
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:00,997
We'll pull through this!

406
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:03,845
And figure out a way to
turn the tables on him?

407
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:38,340
I don't know.

408
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:02,437
Thank you

409
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:09,520
so

410
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:18,899
much for watching.

411
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:37,980
I look forward to serving you again.
